--TEST--
Ordering a `bool` against a number is `E0715`, a chained `1 < 2 < 3` included, since it is `(1 < 2) < 3`; two `bool`s still order (`rule:types/ordering`)
--FILE--
<?nvs
echo (true < 3) as string, "\n";
echo (1 < 2 < 3) as string, "\n";
echo (1.5 <=> false), "\n";
echo (false < true) as string, "\n";
--EXPECT--

--EXPECTF-ERROR--
error[E0715]: `bool` and `int` cannot be ordered
%A
2 | echo (true < 3) as string, "\n";
%A
  = help: a `bool` can be ordered only against another `bool`. To compare three values, write two comparisons joined with `&&`, as in `$a < $b && $b < $c`
%A
error[E0715]: `bool` and `int` cannot be ordered
%A
3 | echo (1 < 2 < 3) as string, "\n";
%A
error[E0715]: `float` and `bool` cannot be ordered
%A
4 | echo (1.5 <=> false), "\n";
%A
error: aborting due to 3 errors
To read what a code means and how to fix it, run `nvs agent show <code>`.
